Instead, the store closed, thanks in part to the self-service grocery revolution launched by Clarence Saunders. Saunders was the self-educated child of impoverished sharecroppers. He eventually found his way to the grocery business in Memphis, Tennessee. He was 35 when he developed the concept for a grocery store that would have no clerks or counters, but instead a labyrinth of aisles that customers would walk themselves, choosing their own food, and placing it in their own shopping baskets. Prices at Saunders' self-service grocery would be lower because his stores would employ
相反，由于克拉伦斯·桑德斯（Clarence Saunders）发起的自助杂货革命，这家店倒闭了。桑德斯是贫困佃农抚养长大、靠自学成才的孩子。他最终在田纳西州孟菲斯市涉足了杂货业。当他构思出一种既没有店员也没有柜台、只有顾客自己走进去挑选食物并放入自己的购物篮的迷宫般通道的杂货店概念时，他35岁。桑德斯的自助杂货店价格会更低，因为他的店铺雇佣的

92
00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:45.000
fewer clerks and also because he wouldn't offer customers credit but instead expect immediate payment. The prices would also be clear and transparent. For the first time, every item in a grocery store would be marked with a price, so customers would no longer fear being overcharged by unscrupulous grocers. Saunders called his grocery store, Piggly Wiggly. Why? Nobody knows. When asked where the name came from, Saunders once answered that it arrived from out of chaos and indirect contact with an individual's mind, which gives you a sense of
店员更少，而且他不再向顾客提供赊账服务，而是期望顾客当场付款。价格也将清晰透明。杂货店里的每件商品将首次标有价格，这样顾客就不再担心被不道德的杂货商多收钱。桑德斯把他的杂货店命名为：皮格利·维格利（Piggly Wiggly）。为什么？没人知道。当被问及这个名字的来历时，桑德斯曾回答说，它是从混沌中以及与个人心灵的间接接触中诞生的，这让你对

93
00:52:45.000 --> 00:53:38.000
the kind of guy he was. But usually, when he was asked why anyone would call a grocery store, Pigley Wiggly, he would answer, so people will ask that very question. The first Pigley Wiggly opened in Memphis in 1916. It was so successful that the second Piggly Wiggly opened three weeks later. Two months after that, another opened. Saunders insisted on calling it, Piggly Wiggly III, to lend his stores the, quote, royal dignity they are due. He soon began attaching a catchphrase to his storefront signs. Piggly Wiggly, all around the world. Of course, at the time, the stores were barely all around Memphis, but Saunders' business did grow phenomenally quickly. Within a year, there were 353 Piggly Wigglies around the United States.
他是个什么样的人有了一个概念。但通常，当别人问他为什么要把一家杂货店叫做“皮格利·维格利”时，他会回答：“这样人们就会问出这个问题。”第一家皮格利·维格利于1916年在孟菲斯开业。它获得了巨大的成功，三周后第二家皮格利·维格利就开业了。两个月后，又一家开业了。桑德斯坚持把它命名为“皮格利·维格利三号”，以赋予他的店铺应有的，引述：“皇室的尊严”。他很快开始在店面招牌上附加一句宣传语：皮格利·维格利，遍及全世界。当然，当时这些店在孟菲斯都还没怎么铺开，但桑德斯的业务确实以惊人的速度增长。一年之内，全美各地就有了353家皮格利·维格利。

