00:53:38.000 --> 00:54:29.000
In newspaper advertisements, Saunders wrote of his self-service concept in nearly Messianic terms. One day, Memphis shall be proud of Piggly Wiggly, one ad-read, and it shall be said by all men that the Piggly Wigglys shall multiply and replenish the earth with more and cleaner things to eat. Another time, he wrote, the mighty pulse of the throbbing today makes new things out of old and new things where was nothing before. Basically, Saunders spoke of Piggly Wiggly as today's Silicon Valley executives talk of their companies. We're not just making money here. We are replenishing the earth. Piggly Wiggly in the self-service grocery stores that followed did lower prices, which meant there was more to eat.
在报纸广告中，桑德斯用近乎弥赛亚般的语言来描述他的自助概念。其中一则广告写道：“总有一天，孟菲斯将为皮格利·维格利感到骄傲，所有人都会说，皮格利·维格利将繁衍并用更多、更干净的食物充满大地。”另一次，他写道：“汹涌的今日之强劲脉搏，将陈旧化为新物，在曾经空无一物的地方创造新物。”基本上，桑德斯谈论皮格利·维格利的方式，就像今天硅谷高管谈论他们的公司一样。我们在这里不只是赚钱。我们在滋养大地。皮格利·维格利以及随之而来的自助杂货店确实降低了价格，这意味着有更多的食物可吃了。

95
00:54:29.000 --> 00:55:10.000
They also changed the kinds of foods that were readily available. To save costs and limit spoilage, Piggly Wiggly stocked less fresh produce than traditional grocery stores. Pre-packaged processed foods became more popular and less expensive, which altered American diets. Brand recognition also became extremely important because food companies had to appeal directly to shoppers, which led to the growth of consumer-oriented food advertising on radio and in newspapers, a phenomenon that Saunders understood better than almost anyone. During the late 19 teens and early 20s, Piggly Wiggly was the single largest newspaper advertiser
它们还改变了随手可得的食物种类。为了节省成本并减少变质，皮格利·维格利储备的新鲜农产品比传统杂货店要少。预包装加工食品变得更受欢迎且更便宜，这改变了美国人的饮食习惯。品牌知名度也变得极为重要，因为食品公司必须直接吸引购物者，这引领了广播和报纸中以消费者为导向的食品广告的发展，这一现象被桑德斯比几乎任何人都理解得更透彻。在1910年代末和20年代初，皮格利·维格利是全美

96
00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:38.000
in the United States. Of course, lower prices and fewer clerks also meant that many people lost their jobs, including my great grandfather. There's nothing new about our fear that automation and increased efficiency will deprive humans of work. In one newspaper advertisement, Saunders imagined a woman torn between her long-time relationship with her friendly grocer, and the woe-woe prices of Pigley Wiggly.
最大的单一报纸广告商。当然，更低的价格和更少的店员也意味着许多人失去了工作，包括我的曾祖父。我们对自动化和提高效率会剥夺人类工作的担忧并不是什么新鲜事。在一则报纸广告中，桑德斯描绘了一个女人在左右为难，她一方面留恋与友好的杂货商长期以来的关系，另一方面又心仪皮格利·维格利那低廉的价格。

97
00:55:38.000 --> 00:56:15.000
The story concluded with Saunders appealing to a tradition even older than the full service grocer, with his protagonist saying, Now away back many years there had been a Dutch grandmother of mine who had been thrifty. The spirit of that old grandmother asserted itself just then within me and said, business is business, and charity and alms are another. Whereupon our shopper saw the light and converted to Piggly Wiggly. By 1922, there were over 1,000 Piggly Wiggly stores around the US, and shares in the company were listed on the New York Stock Exchange.
故事的结局是，桑德斯借助了一个比全套服务杂货商更古老的传统来打动人心，他的主角说道：“很久很久以前，我有一位很节俭的荷兰祖母。那位老祖母的精神当时在我体内苏醒了，并说道：生意归生意，慈善和施舍是另一码事。”于是我们的购物者茅塞顿开，皈依了皮格利·维格利。到1922年，全美各地已有1000多家皮格利·维格利商店，公司的股票也在纽约证券交易所上市。

98
00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:52.000
Saunders was building a 36,000 square foot mansion in Memphis, and had endowed the school now known as Rhodes College. But the good times would not last. After a few pigly wiggly stores in the northeast failed, investors began shorting the stock, betting that its price would fall. Saunders responded by trying to buy up all the available shares of Pigly Wiggly using borrowed money, but the gambit failed spectacularly, and Saunders lost control of Piggly Wiggly and went bankrupt. His vitriol at Wall Street short sellers pre-saged contemporary corporate titans just as his
桑德斯在孟菲斯建造了一座3.6万平方英尺的豪宅，并资助了如今被称为罗兹学院的学校。但好景不长。在东北部的几家皮格利·维格利商店倒闭后，投资者开始做空该股票，押注其价格会下跌。桑德斯的回应是试图通过借来的钱买下所有可流通的皮格利·维格利股票，但这场豪赌以惨败告终，桑德斯失去了对皮格利·维格利公司的控制并宣告破产。他对华尔街做空者的愤怒预示了当代企业巨头们的行径，正如他对

